# Monorepo structure

```
apps/cli            the `crit` binary: argument parsing, terminal UI, wiring. No domain logic.
packages/schema     zod schemas + inferred types + generated JSON Schema. Depends on nothing internal.
packages/store      SQLite persistence (Drizzle, node:sqlite) and repositories. Depends on schema.
packages/mcp        the MCP server agents talk to. Depends on schema.
packages/providers  adapters for Claude Code, Codex, Cursor (+ fake). Depends on schema, store, mcp.
packages/core       the review pipeline: scope, diff, rules, intake, fixes, apply. Depends on schema, store, mcp.
packages/testkit    test helpers (temp git repos, fixtures). Used only from tests.
packages/config     shared tsconfig. No code.
```

## Dependency direction (enforced by review, not just by taste)

`schema` ← `store`, `mcp` ← `core`, `providers` ← `apps/cli`

- A package never imports from a package to its right. `core` does **not** import `providers`: the adapter is
  injected (`ProviderRun`, `AgentRunner`). `apps/cli` is the only place that wires them together.
- `apps/cli` contains no business rules. If a command needs a decision (what to review, how to merge
  findings, how to apply a patch), it belongs in `core`, with a test there.
- A type used by two packages lives in `schema`. Do not export types from `store` or `core` for others to
  depend on.
- New dependencies: justify in the PR; prefer the platform (`node:` modules) over a package.

## Layout inside a package

- Group by **domain**, not by technical role. `core/src/pipeline`, `core/src/rules`, not `core/src/services`
  or `core/src/helpers`.
- One folder per concept once it has 3+ files. A package exposes its public API through its single
  `src/index.ts` entry.
- Keep a file next to what uses it. Promote to a higher level only when a second consumer appears.

## apps/cli layout

`apps/cli/src` is feature-sliced: `app`, `views`, `features`, `shared`. The full rule is in
`.claude/rules/cli/folder-structure.mdc`. A command is a thin file in `app/commands` plus a runner in
`app/runners/<name>`; anything that is a decision belongs in `packages/core`.

## Where tests live

`<package>/test/*.test.ts`. Pure logic gets unit tests next to its package; terminal UI gets Ink tests in
`apps/cli/test`. See the testing rule.
